{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2409 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "71ea4087f0be560239cb9b61c21c2a6974db8bca6d95864d56c71636abf841aa" :edb/db-before-t 2408 :edb/db-after-t 2409 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535721 50 #inst "2026-10-09T05:54:28.524Z" 13194139535721 true] [17592186124420 1020 #edb/ref 17592186363170 13194139535721 true] [17592186124425 1020 #edb/ref 17592186363191 13194139535721 true] [17592186124570 1020 #edb/ref 17592186363177 13194139535721 true] [17592186124570 1020 #edb/ref 17592186363184 13194139535721 true] [17592186124802 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535721 true] [17592186124802 1100 "Given the ellipsoid $((x - 2)^{2})/(12) + ((y + 1)^{2})/(6) + ((z - 1)^{2})/(2) = 1$, find its intercepts with the $x$-axis." 13194139535721 false] [17592186124802 1100 "Given the ellipsoid $\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{12}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{6}+\\frac{(z-1)^{2}}{2}=1$, find its intercepts with the $x$-axis." 13194139535721 true] [17592186124802 1145 "To find the $x$-intercepts, we plug $y=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{12}+\\frac{(0+1)^{2}}{6}+\\frac{(0-1)^{2}}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{12}+\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{1}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{12} & =\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ (x-2)^{2} & =4 \\\\ x-2 & =\\pm 2 \\\\ x & =2\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $x=0$ and $x=4.$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $x$-axis are $(0,0,0)$ and $(4,0,0).$" 13194139535721 true] [17592186363170 1017 #edb/ref 17592186363171 13194139535721 true] [17592186363170 1089 "q-164267" 13194139535721 true] [17592186363170 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535721 true] [17592186363170 1100 "Given the ellipsoid $\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(z-2)^{2}}{16}=1$, find its intercepts with the $y$-axis." 13194139535721 true] [17592186363170 1113 #uuid "50783562-e3df-58d6-82c6-67c9daca87a3" 13194139535721 true] [17592186363170 1145 "To find the $y$-intercepts, we plug $x=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(0+2)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(0-2)^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{4}{8}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{4}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ {y}^{2} & =1 \\\\ y & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $y=-1$ and $y=1.$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $y$-axis are $(0,-1,0)$ and $(0,1,0).$" 13194139535721 true] [17592186363171 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363172 13194139535721 true] [17592186363171 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363173 13194139535721 true] [17592186363171 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363174 13194139535721 true] [17592186363171 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363175 13194139535721 true] [17592186363171 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363176 13194139535721 true] [17592186363171 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535721 true] [17592186363171 1041 "selection" 13194139535721 true] [17592186363171 1104 #edb/ref 17592186363174 13194139535721 true] [17592186363171 1110 #uuid "d757ea12-ef2a-51eb-8f8f-7dbaa93fc0ac" 13194139535721 true] [17592186363172 1034 "$(0,-\\frac{1}{2},0)$ and $(0,1,0)$" 13194139535721 true] [17592186363172 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535721 true] [17592186363172 1111 #uuid "8e252d15-9d72-549a-a170-af1dbe6fe620" 13194139535721 true] [17592186363173 1034 "$(0,0,0)$ and $(0,\\frac{1}{2},0)$" 13194139535721 true] [17592186363173 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535721 true] [17592186363173 1111 #uuid "b6e36100-b9de-54f5-be78-3693c51e2814" 13194139535721 true] [17592186363174 1034 "$(0,-1,0)$ and $(0,1,0)$" 13194139535721 true] [17592186363174 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535721 true] [17592186363174 1111 #uuid "6c645a31-398d-5201-8580-00e944e0d56c" 13194139535721 true] [17592186363175 1034 "$(0,-1,0)$ and $(0,\\frac{1}{2},0)$" 13194139535721 true] [17592186363175 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535721 true] [17592186363175 1111 #uuid "15ce00b9-9977-54ac-930c-a7e4fb034935" 13194139535721 true] [17592186363176 1034 "$(0,-\\frac{1}{2},0)$ and $(0,\\frac{1}{2},0)$" 13194139535721 true] [17592186363176 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535721 true] [17592186363176 1111 #uuid "b19931c3-d2ea-5db7-a60e-3462af3547fb" 13194139535721 true] [17592186363177 1017 #edb/ref 17592186363178 13194139535721 true] [17592186363177 1089 "q-164310" 13194139535721 true] [17592186363177 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535721 true] [17592186363177 1100 "Given the sphere $(x-2)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}+{z}^{2}=5,$ what is the domain of $z=z(x,y)?$" 13194139535721 true] [17592186363177 1113 #uuid "318dfd95-fd1d-563c-ab1e-77dd3f083414" 13194139535721 true] [17592186363177 1145 "From the equation of the sphere, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}+{z}^{2} & =5 \\\\ {z}^{2} & =5-((x-2)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}) \\\\ z & =\\pm \\sqrt{5-((x-2)^{2}+(y+2)^{2})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the square root is defined only for non-negative arguments, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5-((x-2)^{2}+(y+2)^{2})\\ge 0 \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}\\le 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis inequality describes the interior and boundary of the circle \n\n$$\n(x-2)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=5\n$$\n\nwhich is a circle of radius $\\sqrt{5}$ centered at $(2,-2)$ in the $xy$-plane." 13194139535721 true] [17592186363178 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363179 13194139535721 true] [17592186363178 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363180 13194139535721 true] [17592186363178 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363181 13194139535721 true] [17592186363178 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363182 13194139535721 true] [17592186363178 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363183 13194139535721 true] [17592186363178 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535721 true] [17592186363178 1041 "selection" 13194139535721 true] [17592186363178 1104 #edb/ref 17592186363183 13194139535721 true] [17592186363178 1110 #uuid "0ef280cc-6728-5f3d-aaa7-e97f59550f02" 13194139535721 true] [17592186363179 1034 "The interior and boundary of the circle of radius $\\sqrt{5}$  centered at  $(2,2)$" 13194139535721 true] [17592186363179 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535721 true] [17592186363179 1111 #uuid "a199e263-c5ec-51b1-bcbe-94d826ea9f63" 13194139535721 true] [17592186363180 1034 "The interior and boundary of the circle of radius $5$  centered at  $(-2,2)$" 13194139535721 true] [17592186363180 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535721 true] [17592186363180 1111 #uuid "639878ec-d84e-5081-93ae-67f5d766aca9" 13194139535721 true] [17592186363181 1034 "The interior and boundary of the circle of radius $5$  centered at  $(-2,-2)$" 13194139535721 true] [17592186363181 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535721 true] [17592186363181 1111 #uuid "3d095463-aa89-59df-a48b-fd275cd03c95" 13194139535721 true] [17592186363182 1034 "The interior and boundary of the circle of radius $\\sqrt{5}$  centered at  $(-2,2)$" 13194139535721 true] [17592186363182 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535721 true] [17592186363182 1111 #uuid "b3013b1c-db7a-563d-bd7a-d3bc3f1c8191" 13194139535721 true] [17592186363183 1034 "The interior and boundary of the circle of radius $\\sqrt{5}$  centered at  $(2,-2)$" 13194139535721 true] [17592186363183 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535721 true] [17592186363183 1111 #uuid "cfbe648f-9d71-5da5-b518-878f8ba2645d" 13194139535721 true] [17592186363184 1017 #edb/ref 17592186363185 13194139535721 true] [17592186363184 1089 "q-164408" 13194139535721 true] [17592186363184 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535721 true] [17592186363184 1100 "Given the ellipsoid $(x-1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}+\\frac{(z-1)^{2}}{3}=1$, find the domain of $z=z(x,y).$" 13194139535721 true] [17592186363184 1113 #uuid "151fba39-3341-5c5c-87dc-fa3aad0af0b5" 13194139535721 true] [17592186363184 1145 "From the ellipsoid equation, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}+\\frac{(z-1)^{2}}{3} & =1 \\\\ (z+2)^{2} & =3(1-(x-1)^{2}-(y-1)^{2}) \\\\ z+2 & =\\pm \\sqrt{3(1-(x-1)^{2}-(y-1)^{2})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the square root is defined only for non-negative arguments, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-(x-1)^{2}-(y-1)^{2}\\ge 0 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}\\le 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the interior of the circle $(x-1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=1$ and its boundary.\n\nTherefore, the domain is \n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x-1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}\\le 1}.\n$$" 13194139535721 true] [17592186363185 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363186 13194139535721 true] [17592186363185 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363187 13194139535721 true] [17592186363185 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363188 13194139535721 true] [17592186363185 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363189 13194139535721 true] [17592186363185 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363190 13194139535721 true] [17592186363185 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535721 true] [17592186363185 1041 "selection" 13194139535721 true] [17592186363185 1104 #edb/ref 17592186363190 13194139535721 true] [17592186363185 1110 #uuid "994816f4-574d-5806-a422-55714416164e" 13194139535721 true] [17592186363186 1034 "{(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<1}" 13194139535721 true] [17592186363186 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535721 true] [17592186363186 1111 #uuid "318be70c-85dc-57c5-b586-5ac051526996" 13194139535721 true] [17592186363187 1034 "{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x-1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}\\le \\frac{1}{3}}" 13194139535721 true] [17592186363187 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535721 true] [17592186363187 1111 #uuid "d6742970-de21-529f-82b3-8177313cb8b9" 13194139535721 true] [17592186363188 1034 "{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x-1)^{2}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{3}\\le 1}" 13194139535721 true] [17592186363188 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535721 true] [17592186363188 1111 #uuid "472615e4-d73b-5b00-b451-7fceea139314" 13194139535721 true] [17592186363189 1034 "{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x-1)^{2}+{y}^{2}>1}" 13194139535721 true] [17592186363189 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535721 true] [17592186363189 1111 #uuid "b1a316c0-78f3-54ce-b430-d32da07fb576" 13194139535721 true] [17592186363190 1034 "{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x-1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}\\le 1}" 13194139535721 true] [17592186363190 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535721 true] [17592186363190 1111 #uuid "387089d1-90ef-50ee-beb5-9f0844